ost sits, not a finding yet.\n- **Why it's provisional:**\n  - At 8 beads the stamped copy lost 138–144 frames, against 15–16 for the unstamped S1. My guess is that the stamp calls run on LabVIEW's UI thread and slow the loops. That thread setting has not been read yet.\n  - I first wrote that \"the kernel does not grow\". The retrospective showed that is not supported: at 8 beads the loop is paced by the camera (11.14 ms against 11.11 ms per frame), so those times are mostly waiting for the frame. I withdrew the claim in the plan (198(b)) and in STATUS.\n- **Retrospective:** one fault, `inference-over-measurement`, costing about 15 min and $1.27. The bead-count check used an exact decimal comparison and was never tried on an existing output file. It flagged a correct 15-bead leg as wrong, which caused one needless rerun, and the step-4 card ran 95 min against a 75 min budget. I accepted the fault and annotated the review.\n- **Next cycle's first act** (`next.json`, plan 198(c)), all measurements:\n  - read the thread setting of the 12 stamps;\n  - run one 8-bead leg on the unstamped S1;\n  - log which window holds the mouse capture when the first bead click is lost;\n  - test any leg-gating check against an existing output file before launch.\n- **Not done this cycle:** the bgrun repair card (`task_91-2.json`, still owed from cycle 90) is valid but was not dispatched because the time ran out. It comes right after the first act, together with capturing the Quit dialog before LabVIEW is force-closed.\n- **For the user:** decision D-2026-09-26-01 (loop-level timers only) is still open; work continues under its recommendation. The permission layer blocked the text fix for `.claude/agents/material*.md`, which still tell sub-sessions to use the refused `MATERIAL=1` prefix. The replacement text is in `tools/bench/audit_c7_agent_patch.md` for you to apply.","ttft_ms":2012,"type":"result","duration_ms":8836554,"uuid":"23aa4c95-5c85-4412-ba03-745389b84d6c","ttft_stream_ms":1